   "he": "אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בְּרַבִּי צָדוֹק: מַעֲשֶׂה בְּבַת כֹּהֵן שֶׁזִּינְּתָה וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף: בֵּית דִּין שֶׁל צַדּוּקִים הֲוָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Elazar, son of Rabbi Tzadok, said: An incident» occurred «with regard to a priest’s daughter who committed adultery,» and she was executed by actual burning, and the Sages said to him that the court at that time was not proficient in halakha. «Rav Yosef says: It was a court of the Sadducees,» who interpreted the verse according to its straightforward meaning."
  }
